      </table>

      <h2 id="best-overall-make">#1 — Make (Best Overall Zapier Alternative)</h2>
      <p>Make (formerly Integromat) is the best overall Zapier alternative because its visual scenario builder handles complex branching, routing, iteration, and error recovery more intuitively than Zapier's linear Paths. At $9/month for 10,000 operations, Make delivers roughly 3–5x the automation volume per dollar compared to Zapier at equivalent pricing. For teams with multi-step workflows, Make's pricing model is significantly more cost-effective.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is the learning curve. Make's visual builder is more powerful but more complex than Zapier's trigger-action model. Teams used to Zapier's simplicity may need 1–2 weeks to adapt. For the full breakdown, see <a href="/reviews/zapier-vs-make/">Zapier vs Make</a>.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Make</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Visual scenario builder</strong> — Drag-and-drop modules with visual branching and routing</li>
          <li><strong>1,800+ app integrations</strong> — Native connectors plus HTTP and API modules</li>
          <li><strong>Operation-based pricing</strong> — 10,000 ops/mo at $9 (vs Zapier's 750 tasks at $19.99)</li>
          <li><strong>Error handling</strong> — Breakpoints, fallback routes, and resume-on-error</li>
          <li><strong>Free tier</strong> — 1,000 operations/month, unlimited scenarios</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://make.com" class="btn-alt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Try Make Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-selfhosted-n8n">#2 — n8n (Best Self-Hosted / Open-Source)</h2>
      <p>n8n is the best Zapier alternative for teams that want full control over their automation infrastructure. Self-hosted n8n is free with no operation limits — you run it on your own server (Docker, npm, or cloud VM). The workflow builder supports branching, merging, code nodes (JavaScript), and webhooks. For teams with technical capacity, n8n delivers the lowest total cost of ownership in the automation space.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is hosting and maintenance. Self-hosting requires Docker knowledge and server management. n8n Cloud at $20/month removes the hosting burden but introduces operation limits. The app directory (400+ integrations) is smaller than Make or Zapier.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>n8n</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Self-hosted free</strong> — No operation limits, no subscription, full source code on GitHub</li>
          <li><strong>Visual workflow builder</strong> — Nodes, branching, merging, and code nodes</li>
          <li><strong>JavaScript code nodes</strong> — Custom logic, data transformation, and API calls</li>
          <li><strong>400+ integrations</strong> — Plus custom HTTP nodes for any REST API</li>
          <li><strong>Fair-code license</strong> — Free for self-hosting, paid for cloud and enterprise</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://n8n.io" class="btn-alt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Get n8n Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-developers-pipedream">#3 — Pipedream (Best for Developers & APIs)</h2>
      <p>Pipedream is the best Zapier alternative for developers who want to write code in their automations. Every step in a Pipedream workflow can include Node.js, Python, Go, or Bash code. The platform handles authentication, rate limiting, and webhook management so developers can focus on logic. For API-heavy workflows, Pipedream is the most developer-friendly automation platform.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is that Pipedream is code-first — non-technical team members will find it harder to use than Make or Zapier. The free tier (100 invocations/day) is suitable for development but may not cover production workloads.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Pipedream</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Code-first workflows</strong> — Node.js, Python, Go, and Bash in every step</li>
          <li><strong>2,500+ API integrations</strong> — Pre-built auth for most popular APIs</li>
          <li><strong>Webhook triggers</strong> — Native HTTP endpoints for incoming webhooks</li>
          <li><strong>Scheduled triggers</strong> — Cron-based and interval-based triggers</li>
          <li><strong>Free tier</strong> — 100 invocations/day, unlimited workflows</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://pipedream.com" class="btn-alt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Try Pipedream Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-simplicity-integrately">#4 — Integrately (Best for Simplicity & Value)</h2>
      <p>Integrately is the best Zapier alternative for non-technical users who want 1-click automations. Integrately offers pre-built integration recipes — "When X happens in app A, do Y in app B" — that you activate with a single click. For small teams that need basic automations without learning a workflow builder, Integrately is the simplest and most affordable option.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is depth. Integrately supports fewer apps than Zapier or Make, and complex multi-step workflows with branching logic are harder to build. The platform is best for simple 1:1 automations, not sophisticated integration pipelines.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Integrately</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>1-click automations</strong> — Pre-built recipes for common integration patterns</li>
          <li><strong>20,000+ pre-built workflows</strong> — Largest library of ready-to-use automations</li>
          <li><strong>Visual builder</strong> — Drag-and-drop for custom workflows</li>
          <li><strong>Affordable pricing</strong> — $19.99/mo for 3,000 tasks (vs Zapier $19.99 for 750)</li>
          <li><strong>Free tier</strong> — 300 tasks/month, 5 active integrations</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://integrately.com" class="btn-alt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Try Integrately Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-microsoft-power-automate">#5 — Microsoft Power Automate (Best for Microsoft 365)</h2>
      <p>Microsoft Power Automate is the best Zapier alternative for organizations on Microsoft 365. It is included in most M365 plans (Power Automate Seeded) at no additional cost, integrates natively with SharePoint, Teams, Outlook, Dynamics 365, and Power BI, and supports desktop RPA for legacy applications. For enterprises, Power Automate is often the lowest-cost option because it is already paid for.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is the app directory. Power Automate's connector library for non-Microsoft services (1,000+ connectors) is smaller than Zapier's 7,000+, and the workflow builder is less intuitive than Make's visual canvas.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Microsoft Power Automate</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Included in M365</strong> — No additional cost for most Microsoft 365 plans</li>
          <li><strong>1,000+ connectors</strong> — Native Microsoft + third-party connectors</li>
          <li><strong>Desktop RPA</strong> — UI automation for legacy desktop applications</li>
          <li><strong>AI Builder</strong> — Built-in AI for document extraction, sentiment, and prediction</li>
          <li><strong>Enterprise security</strong> — DLP, data loss prevention, and environment isolation</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://flow.microsoft.com" class="btn-alt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Try Power Automate</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="selection-scenarios">Selection Scenarios</h2>

      <div class="use-case">
        <h3>Startup / Small Team (Simple Automations)</h3>
        <p><strong>Recommendation: Make Free or Integrately Free.</strong> Make's free tier (1,000 ops/mo) handles 3–5 active workflows. Integrately is even simpler with 1-click recipes. Upgrade when you exceed free-tier limits or need branching logic.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="use-case">
        <h3>Technical Team (Developer-Heavy)</h3>
        <p><strong>Recommendation: n8n (self-hosted) or Pipedream.</strong> n8n gives unlimited operations for free if you host it. Pipedream is best if your workflows are API-heavy and you want to write code in each step. Both are code-first and best for teams with JavaScript skills.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="use-case">
        <h3>Enterprise on Microsoft 365</h3>
        <p><strong>Recommendation: Microsoft Power Automate (included).</strong> If you already pay for M365, Power Automate is free and integrates natively with your Microsoft stack. Reserve Zapier or Make for non-Microsoft integrations that Power Automate does not support.</p>
      </div>

