      <h2 id="buying-guide">Buying Guide: How to Choose a Zapier Alternative in 2026</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Step 1 — Count your monthly operations:</strong> Zapier charges per task. Make charges per operation. n8n is free if self-hosted. Knowing your volume determines which pricing model is cheapest.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 2 — Check app directory:</strong> Verify that every app you need to connect has a native integration. Zapier leads with 7,000+ apps; Make has 1,800+; n8n has 400+ but supports any REST API via HTTP nodes.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 3 — Evaluate workflow complexity:</strong> If you need branching, routing, error handling, and code — Make, n8n, or Pipedream. If you need simple 1:1 automations — Integrately or Zapier.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 4 — Test the free tier:</strong> Make, n8n, Pipedream, and Integrately all have free tiers. Build one real workflow and test for a week before paying.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 5 — Consider self-hosting:</strong> If you have a developer and want zero operation limits, n8n self-hosted is the cheapest long-term option.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Learn more about our <a href="/how-we-test/">testing methodology</a> and <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>What is the best free alternative to Zapier in 2026?</summary>
          <p>Make (formerly Integromat) offers a free tier with 1,000 operations per month, which is the most generous free tier among visual automation builders. n8n is free if you self-host, with no operation limits. For developers, Pipedream offers 100 free invocations per day. For non-technical users who want a visual builder, Make's free tier is the best starting point.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is Make better than Zapier?</summary>
          <p>Make is better than Zapier for teams that need complex multi-step workflows, visual branching logic, and lower per-operation pricing. Make's visual scenario builder handles routers, iterators, error handlers, and filters more intuitively than Zapier's Paths. Zapier is better for teams that prioritize the largest app directory (7,000+ apps) and the simplest setup experience.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can n8n replace Zapier for a small team?</summary>
          <p>n8n can replace Zapier for a small team that has basic technical skills or a developer on staff. Self-hosted n8n is free with no operation limits, and the workflow builder supports branching, merging, code nodes, and webhooks. The trade-off is that self-hosting requires server setup and maintenance. n8n Cloud starts at $20/month and eliminates the hosting burden.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which automation tool is best for Microsoft 365 teams?</summary>
          <p>Microsoft Power Automate is the best automation tool for teams already on Microsoft 365. It is included in most M365 plans at no additional cost, integrates natively with SharePoint, Teams, Outlook, Dynamics, and Power BI, and supports RPA (desktop automation) for legacy systems. The trade-off is that Power Automate's app directory for non-Microsoft services is smaller than Zapier's or Make's.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

